<p class="sub-head"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:normal;"><a name="Display_Settings"></a>Display Settings</span></i></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The options in both Display and Ranges sections allow the user to customise the visualisation of the inspected surfaces. All changes can be applied to the current page or to all pages.</span></p>
<table class="TableGrid" style="border:none; left:0px; top:1378px; width:704px; border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0" width="704">
<col class="whs37">
<col class="whs38">
<tr class="whs39">
<td rowspan="5" valign="top" width="215px" class="whs40">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/inspection_pane_7.gif" width="200px" height="140px" border="0" class="img_whs41" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" width="446px" class="whs42">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reference</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> select a display mode for the reference entity. Six modes are available:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>None</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> does not display the reference at all.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Boundary</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> displays the reference as boundary. This option is available only for pages aligned to cross sections.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Flat</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> displays the reference in flat shaded mode.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Smooth</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> displays the reference in smooth shaded mode.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Flat and transparent</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> displays the reference in flat shaded mode with transparency.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Smooth and transparent</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> displays the reference in smooth shaded mode with transparency.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Note:</b> The transparency for the last two modes is controlled from <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; General</b></i></span> tab - <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Inspection mode rendering</b></span> group.</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs43">
<td valign="top" width="446px" class="whs44">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point size</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- the size of a scan point in screen points. This option is enabled only when the rendering of the compared entity is Large points.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs45">
<td valign="top" width="446px" class="whs44">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Backfacing points</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- draws points with reversed normals.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs46">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top" width="446px" class="whs47">
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Render points in zero range</b></span> - enables displaying the points of the central tolerance band. By default this option is ON, so all compared points will be displayed. If the option is OFF, then all points in the zero range will be invisible.</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs46">
<td valign="top" width="446px" class="whs47">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Error scale</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- scales the error vector length. This option is enabled only in pages aligned to cross sections.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:normal;"><a name="Ranges_section"></a>Ranges section</span></i></p>
<table class="TableGrid" style="border:none; left:0px; top:2033px; width:704px; border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0" width="704">
<col class="whs48">
<col class="whs49">
<tr class="whs50">
<td rowspan="2" valign="top" width="216px" class="whs51">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/inspection_pane_8.gif" width="199px" height="80px" border="0" class="img_whs52" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" width="445px" class="whs53">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Next two options define the range of the colour scale.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Max</span> - the upper border of the colour scale. All points, higher than this value will be coloured as Above Max values.</b></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Min</span> - the lower border of the colour scale. All points, lower than this value will be coloured as Below Min values.</b></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs54">
<td valign="top" width="445px" class="whs55">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">T</span><span lang="EN-US">he next two properties define the zero range - all points within this range will be coloured as zero points.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Max Zero</span> - the upper border of the zero range.</b></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Min Zero</span> - the lower border of the zero range.</b></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Note:</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">The minus sign for the Min values in this section is not taken for granted, so you need to type it if you mean it.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:normal;"><a name="Buttons"></a>Buttons</span></i></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="708" class="whs56">
<col class="whs57">
<col class="whs58">
<tr valign="top" class="whs24">
<td width="13.839%" class="whs59">
